          "rawQuery": true,
          "rawSql": "SELECT\n  b.time AS time,\n  l.label AS sensor,\n  b.conductivity_us_cm\nFROM bt_readings b\nJOIN sensors s ON s.id = b.sensor_id\nLEFT JOIN sensor_labels l ON l.sensor_id = b.sensor_id\nWHERE\n  $__timeFilter(b.time)\n  AND s.kind = 'bt' AND s.active = true\n  AND b.conductivity_us_cm IS NOT NULL\nORDER BY b.time",
          "refId": "A",
          "sql": {
            "columns": [
              {
                "parameters": [],
                "type": "function"
              }
            ],
            "groupBy": [
              {
                "property": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "type": "groupBy"
              }
            ],
            "limit": 50
          }
        }
      ],
      "title": "BLE Soil Conductivity (\u00b5S/cm)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "description": "Fertiliser salts in the soil, measured as conductivity between the probe's two electrodes. Read it together with moisture: EC collapses toward zero in dry soil regardless of how much fertiliser is present, so a low line on a dry pot means \"dry\", not \"hungry\". The feed_needed alert only trusts EC above 20% moisture for exactly this reason. Thresholds are per-plant (min_soil_ec), so there is no single line to draw here \u2014 compare each series against its own plant's minimum."
    },
